//    adxContValid: 40 → 60 ; volChopLow default: 1.5 → 2.5
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 9.5".
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v9.5 — 2026-06-21 — Volume ceiling → chop carve-out (data-driven, 540 pre-ceiling high-vol trades)
//
//  ROOT CAUSE: v8.0's flat volumeNotExcess = volume < 1.5× volMa blocked ALL high-volume
//  bars. But for a CALL, a high-volume bar IS the breakout. The data (pre-ceiling) shows:
//    - 1.5-2.0×: 58% win, +0.78   |  2.0-2.5×: 55% win, +1.47   (good, were blocked)
//    - 2.5-3.0×: 37% win, -1.42   (the ONLY bad band — the real chop/blowoff zone)
//    - 3.0-4.0×: 59% win, +2.27   |  4.0×+: 58% win, +5.05      (best breakouts, were blocked)
//  Post-Jun-17 the flat ceiling fired 0 high-vol trades — it threw out the +5% breakouts
//  to avoid one bad band.
//
//  FIX: volumeNotExcess = pass below volChopLow OR at/above volChopHigh; block only the
//    volChopLow-volChopHigh chop band. Defaults 2.5 / 3.0. Lets explosive breakouts (>3×)
//    and moderate volume (<2.5×) through; blocks only the 2.5-3.0× blowoff zone.
//  NOTE: pre-ceiling evidence, smaller samples — watch 2-3 days before trusting fully.
//
//  TO REVERT v9.5 → v9.4:
//    volumeNotExcess = volume < volMa * volCeilMultiplier
//    Delete volChopLow / volChopHigh inputs.
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 9.4".
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v9.4 — 2026-06-18 — Simplified unified flip trigger (DEEP + CONT context split)
//
//  CONCEPT: Replace the complex deepReversalTrigger + momentumAccelTrigger with
//  a single shared burst detection block, split only by MACD context:
//    macdLine[1] <= 0  →  DEEP_MACD_REVERSAL   (recovery from bearish territory)
//    macdLine[1] >  0  →  MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION (pullback resumption in uptrend)
//
//  Removed gates: deepContext (was closing window), deepReversalSetup,
//  sustainedHistRise, bbFilter, sessionRisingFilter, momentumAccelSetup,
//  stockNotOverextended (blocks gap-up stocks already 1%+ before open).
//
//  CHANGES vs v9.3:
//  1. earlyFlipBurst: shared burst detection for both contexts
//       histShiftPrevBar (3-bar window) + hist[1]>=0.05 + hist>=1.6x + close>open
//       + volume > volume[1] (rising bar-over-bar) + volumeNotExcess
//  2. earlyFlipQuality: shared quality gates
//       rsiRecovery + vwapRising + emaTrendFlexible + adxDeepValid
//       + noUpperReject + close>dayOpen + inTradeWindow + isExpectedTimeframe
//  3. deepReversalTrigger  = earlyFlipBurst + earlyFlipQuality + macdLine[1] <= 0
//  4. earlyContFlipTrigger = earlyFlipBurst + earlyFlipQuality + macdLine[1] > 0
//     (added to momentumContinuationTrigger OR — existing hist>0.60 path kept)
//  5. momentumAccelTrigger removed (covered by earlyContFlipTrigger)
//  6. stockNotOverextended removed from all triggers
//
//  TO REVERT v9.4 → v9.3:
//    Restore deepReversalTrigger to its v9.3 definition (deepReversalSetup and ...)
//    Remove earlyFlipBurst, earlyFlipQuality, earlyContFlipTrigger variables
//    Restore momentumAccelTrigger
//    Add stockNotOverextended back to CONT trigger
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 9.3"
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v9.3 — 2026-06-18 — Early DEEP entry: volume + flip-window fixes
//
//  ROOT CAUSE: PIIND/M&M/EICHERMOT entered at candle 10 instead of candle 2.
//  1-min candle replay for all 3 stocks showed DEEP gate conditions were met
//  at bar 1 (9:30/9:27 respectively) — ONLY blocker was volumeBurstCandle2:
//    volume > volMa (100% threshold) vs continuationVolumeCandle2 = volMa * 0.9
//  Early-session bars (9:27-9:31) routinely come in at 85-90% of rolling vol MA.
//  CONT already uses 0.9x — DEEP was needlessly stricter.
//
//  Second issue: histShiftPrevBar was a 1-bar-only window (exactly 1 bar ago).
//  If bar 1 misses for any reason (bloom/wick), the DEEP path closes forever
//  and entry waits for hist > 0.60 (CONT threshold) = candle 10+.
//  Fix: extend to 3-bar window — flip detected within last 3 bars.
//
//  CHANGES vs v9.2:
//  1. volumeBurstCandle2: volume > volMa → volumeNotExcess  (floor removed)
//     volMa = ta.sma(volume, 20) at 09:27-09:30 includes previous day's high-
//     volume close bars → inflates SMA → PIIND bar1 was 0.39x MA, M&M was 0.75x.
//     The ceiling (volumeNotExcess) already blocks the 9% WR panic spikes.
//     deepContext + histBurstCandle2 + bloomingCandle provide sufficient quality.
//  2. histShiftPrevBar: exact-1-bar → within-3-bar window
//     If bar1 misses (bloom/wick/other), bar2 and bar3 still get a DEEP chance
//     instead of waiting for hist > 0.60 (CONT threshold = candle 10+).
//
//  TO REVERT v9.3 → v9.2:
//    volumeBurstCandle2: restore to: volume > volMa and volumeNotExcess
//    histShiftPrevBar: restore to single-bar: macdHist[2] <= 0 and macdHist[1] > 0
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 9.2"
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v9.2 — 2026-06-18 — Gap-up stock fixes from top-gainers live analysis
//
//  ROOT CAUSE: 0/9 top gainers fired today (CDSL +8%, NYKAA +6%, etc).
//  Three systematic blockers identified via analyze_pine_filters.py:
//
//  1. stockNotOverextended used dayChange from PREV close → gap-up stocks
//     blocked from minute 1 (CDSL +8% → blocked all day despite being up
//     only +1% from today's open). Fix: use intradayChange (from dayOpen).
//
//  2. adxContValid upper cap = 40 → all strong-trend stocks have ADX 40-100.
//     ADX > 40 means STRONG trend, not exhausted. Fix: raise cap to 60.
//
//  3. ACCEL + CONT require MACD flip (histShiftPrevBar) → stocks trending from
//     open with consistently positive MACD never get a flip after ~9:37.
//     Fix: sustained bypass — if hist > 0.60 AND rising 3+ bars AND hist
//     rising over 2 bars, skip the flip requirement.
//
//  CHANGES vs v9.0:
//  1. intradayChange: new variable = (close - dayOpen) / dayOpen * 100
//     stockNotOverextended: now uses intradayChange < 3% (was dayChange < 3%)
//     stockDayWinner: still uses dayChange >= 0.25% from prev close (unchanged)
//  2. adxContValid: upper cap 40 → 60
//  3. accelHistValid: momentumHistAccel OR (continuationSequenceReady AND
//     sustainedHistRise AND macdHistRising) — replaces momentumHistAccel in ACCEL
//  4. combinedContReady: contBurstReady OR (continuationSequenceReady AND
//     sustainedHistRise AND macdHistRising) — replaces contBurstReady in CONT
//
//  TO REVERT v9.2 → v9.0:
//    Delete intradayChange line
//    stockNotOverextended: change intradayChange back to dayChange
//    adxContValid: change upper cap 60 back to 40
//    Delete accelHistValid line; replace accelHistValid with momentumHistAccel in ACCEL trigger
//    Delete combinedContReady line; replace combinedContReady with contBurstReady in CONT trigger
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 9.0"
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v9.0 — 2026-06-17 — Candle confirmation + COCHINSHIP missed-signal fixes
//
//  ROOT CAUSE: v8.0 was still missing valid setups (COCHINSHIP 11:59):
//    stockDayWinner=0.50% too strict — blocks stocks +0.36% on neutral NIFTY days
//    bloomingCandle had close<bbUpper which blocks breakout candles (price piercing
//    BB upper is the SIGNAL, not a reason to skip)
//    No candle-level confirmation to verify trend continuation for next 5-8 bars
//
//  CHANGES vs v8.0:
//  1. stockDayWinner: 0.50% → 0.25% for CONTINUATION
//     Rational: on NIFTY +0.27% day, requiring +0.50% day-change is too strict.
//  2. bloomingCandle: removed "and close < bbUpper"
//     Rational: stockNotOverextended (dayChange < 3%) already caps fading entries.
//     Breakout candles legitimately pierce BB upper.
//  3. Signal-specific candle confirmation (lightweight, no new indicators):
//     DEEP:         noUpperReject = upper wick < body — sellers couldn't push back
//     CONTINUATION: closeInUpperHalf = close > (high+low)/2 — buying pressure dominated
//     ACCEL:        rangeExpansion (already defined) — surge bar must be above-avg range
//
//  TO REVERT v9.0 → v8.0:
//    stockDayWinner: change 0.25 back to 0.50

//    bloomingCandle: add "and close < bbUpper" back
//    Remove "noUpperReject" from deepReversalTrigger
//    Remove "closeInUpperHalf" from momentumContinuationTrigger
//    Remove "rangeExpansion" from momentumAccelTrigger
//    Delete definitions of noUpperReject and closeInUpperHalf
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 8.0"
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v8.0 — 2026-06-17 — Full redesign from PGEL/KEI/SWIGGY 1-min candle analysis
//
//  ROOT CAUSE: v7.5 was blocking ALL early-momentum entries on trend days.
//    histFloor=0.30 blocked 1st candle of zero-cross (orig 0.05)
//    histContMCFloor=0.80 on CONTINUATION fired AFTER the move, not at bloom
//    continuationSequenceReady floor=1.00 too aggressive for mid-level DEEP setups
//    priceBurstCandle2=open>close[1] was a dead gate (true 95% of bars)
//
//  CHANGES vs v7.5:
//  1. histFloor: 0.30 → 0.05 (original). 1.5× burst multiplier on candle 2 is the real gate.
//  2. DEEP: continuationSequenceReady floor 1.00 → 0.60. ADX > 15 gate added.
//     RSI overbought escape (rsi > 75) removed — overbought = fading, not blooming.
//  3. priceBurstCandle2: replaced dead gate (open>close[1]) with bloomingCandle
//     (bullish body ≥ avg body, close > EMA9).
//  4. MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION: full redesign.
//     OLD: macdHist >= 0.80 floor → fired late, entered fades.
//     NEW: same 3-candle burst logic as DEEP + directional RSI (rising, 40-78)
//          + ADX 18-40 + volume ≥ 1.0× avg.
//  5. ADX indicator added (ta.dmi 14,14). DEEP uses adxVal > 15, CONT uses 18-40.
//
//  Signal logic separation post-v8.0:
//    DEEP:         macdLine≤0 AND macdSignal≤0 → burst from deep negative
//    CONTINUATION: stockDayWinner (≥0.25%) + brief dip → MACD zero-cross burst
//    ACCEL:        MACD consistently positive → continuationSequenceReady (hist>0.60)
//
//  TO REVERT v8.0 → v7.5:
//    histFloor: 0.05 → 0.30
//    continuationSequenceReady floor: 0.60 → 1.00
//    priceBurstCandle2: bloomingCandle → open > close[1]
//    rsiRecovery: add back "or rsi > 75"
//    Remove ADX lines (ta.dmi + adxDeepValid + adxContValid)
//    Restore CONTINUATION to: contHistStrong = macdHist >= histContMCFloor (0.80) gate
//    Change indicator title back to "Sniper CE 7.5"
//
// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// v7.5 — 2026-06-16 — Data-driven from 253-signal backtest (81 symbols, 7 days)
//  1. MACD_REVERSAL disabled (9% WR at all hist levels)
//  2. MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION: added macdHist >= 0.80 floor (WR 24%→44%)
//  3. continuationSequenceReady: hard floor 0.50 → 1.00 (DEEP WR 46%→67%)
//  Net: 253 → 50 signals/week, WR 21% → 46%, total -5.5% → +6.5%
//
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

//──────── INPUTS ────────
emaFast             = input.int(9, "EMA Fast")
emaSlow             = input.int(20, "EMA Slow")
rsiLen              = input.int(14, "RSI Length")
rsiMin              = input.float(40.0, "RSI Min Entry (Reversal)")
macdFast            = input.int(12, "MACD Fast")
macdSlow            = input.int(26, "MACD Slow")
macdSignalLen       = input.int(9, "MACD Signal")
bbLen               = input.int(20, "BB Length")
bbStd               = input.float(2.0, "BB StdDev")
volMaLen            = input.int(20, "Volume MA Length")
volMultiplier       = input.float(1.2, "Volume Multiplier")
niftySymbol         = input.symbol("NSE:NIFTY", "NIFTY Symbol")
// v8.0: reverted 0.30 → 0.05 (original). The 1.5× burst multiplier on candle 2 is the real gate.
histFloor           = input.float(0.05, "Histogram Floor Magnitude")
// v9.14 added price-scaled floor scaling here; v9.19 REMOVED it from the burst gates (DIXON/SHREECEM
// showed price is a bad proxy for histogram amplitude — see v9.18/v9.19 changelog). Back to the flat
// histFloor above. Kept only for input-panel compatibility, same as histContMCFloor below.
histFloorPricePct   = input.float(0.01, "Histogram Floor (% of price) [UNUSED v9.19]") / 100
// v9.15 CRITICAL FIX: 1.5x/2.0x bar-over-bar was NEVER satisfied on real 1-min data — confirmed by
// live debug run 2026-07-03: EVERY bloomingCandle bar on 3 different stocks (UPL, SONA BLW, BHARAT
// FORGE), full sessions, showed "BURST✗" — the burst ratio was the sole, universal blocker; the
// confluence gates (RSI/Vol/EMA/ADX/VWAP) were never even reached. Root cause: MACD histogram is a
// smoothed oscillator (difference of two EMAs, itself further smoothed by the signal EMA) — a 50-100%
// jump between two ADJACENT 1-min candles is an extreme, rare event, not what a normal ignition looks
// like. Recalibrated to thresholds a genuine acceleration can actually clear: 1.15x/1.3x instead of
// 1.5x/2.0x. Still requires real, directional acceleration (not a flat/noisy tick) — just not an
// unrealistic one.
histBurstMultiplier = input.float(1.15, "Histogram Burst Multiplier")
contStrongMult      = input.float(1.3, "Continuation Strong Burst Multiplier (candle-2 fire)")
// Data-driven: 9% WR disaster when vol > 1.5× with MACD 0.3-0.5
volCeilMultiplier   = input.float(1.5, "Volume Ceiling Multiplier [UNUSED v9.5]")
// v9.6: chop carve-out widened down to 1.5× — the 1.5-2.5× band was 13% win / -81% in live
// forward test (chasing volume on late entries). Block 1.5-3.0×; allow <1.5× normal and
// >=3.0× explosive breakouts only.
volChopLow          = input.float(1.5, "Volume Chop Band Low (×volMa)")
volChopHigh         = input.float(3.0, "Volume Chop Band High (×volMa)")
// v9.12: 3% → 6% — the 3% intraday cap was blocking the actual top gainers (+4-8%) entirely.
dayChangeCeil       = input.float(6.0, "Day Change Ceiling %")
// v8.0: histContMCFloor is no longer used in CONTINUATION trigger (replaced by contBurstReady).
// Kept here to preserve TradingView input panel compatibility. Has no effect on signals.
histContMCFloor     = input.float(0.80, "Continuation MC Hist Floor [UNUSED v8.0]")
// v7.5: MACD_REVERSAL (neutral context) = 9% WR in backtest — disabled by default.
// Set true only for research/debugging to see where alerts would have fired.
enableMACDReversal  = input.bool(false, "Enable MACD Reversal (9% WR, disabled)")
showLabels          = input.bool(true, "Show Labels")
isExpectedTimeframe = timeframe.isminutes and timeframe.multiplier == 1

//──────── CORE INDICATORS ────────
ema9   = ta.ema(close, emaFast)
ema20  = ta.ema(close, emaSlow)
rsi    = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
[macdLine, macdSignal, macdHist] = ta.macd(close, macdFast, macdSlow, macdSignalLen)
[bbUpper, bbMiddle, bbLower] = ta.bb(close, bbLen, bbStd)
bbWidth  = (bbUpper - bbLower) / bbMiddle * 100
volMa    = ta.sma(volume, volMaLen)
// v8.0: ADX for trend bloom vs exhaustion gate
[diPlus, diMinus, adxVal] = ta.dmi(14, 14)
vwapVal  = ta.vwap(hlc3)
// v9.14: dayOpen computed locally (var, zero repaint) instead of request.security("D", open, ...).
// The security() form is correct in REALTIME but on historical/replay bars it lags a full day
// (HTF values only resolve once the daily bar closes) — every bar-replay audit ("why did/didn't
// this fire at 11:59") was silently checked against YESTERDAY's open/close. Live production alerts
// were never affected (security() resolves the forming daily bar correctly intrabar in realtime),
// but this removes the ambiguity entirely so future replay-based tuning is trustworthy.
var float dayOpen = na
if ta.change(time("D")) != 0
    dayOpen := open
// close[1] offset is immune to repaint even with lookahead_on (the standard safe HTF-close pattern)
// and — unlike lookahead_off — resolves correctly on historical/replay bars too.
prevDayClose  = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", close[1], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
nifty50PrevClose = request.security(niftySymbol, "D", close[1], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
// nifty50Close (today's still-forming close) keeps lookahead_off — correct live; same one-day-lag
// caveat as dayOpen applies only to replay of the market_trend telemetry field, not to live alerts.
nifty50Close     = request.security(niftySymbol, "D", close,    barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_off)
nifty50Change    = nifty50PrevClose > 0 ? (nifty50Close - nifty50PrevClose) / nifty50PrevClose * 100 : 0
dayChange        = prevDayClose > 0 ? (close - prevDayClose) / prevDayClose * 100 : na
// v9.2: intraday extension measured from today's open, not yesterday's close.
// Gap-up stocks (CDSL +7%) were blocked all day by the old dayChange-based check.
// A stock up 7% from yesterday but only +1% from today's open is NOT overextended.
intradayChange   = dayOpen > 0 ? (close - dayOpen) / dayOpen * 100 : na

//──────── DATA-DRIVEN GATES ────────
// Both gates derived from 84-trade analysis. Override/tune via inputs above.
// v9.5: chop carve-out — block only the 2.5-3.0× blowoff band; allow moderate AND explosive volume.
volumeNotExcess = volume < volMa * volChopLow or volume >= volMa * volChopHigh
// v9.2: uses intradayChange (from today's open) — gap-up stocks no longer blocked from bar 1
stockNotOverextended = na(intradayChange) or intradayChange < dayChangeCeil

//──────── TREND FILTER ────────
macdHistRising   = ta.rising(macdHist, 2)
emaTrendStrict   = ema9 > ema20 and ema20 > ema20[1]
emaTrendFlexible = ema9 > ema20 or macdHistRising
emaSupport       = low >= ema9 or close > ema9
emaSlope         = ema9 > ema9[1] and ema9[1] > ema9[2]
trendFilterStrict   = emaTrendStrict and emaSupport and emaSlope
trendFilterFlexible = emaTrendFlexible and emaSupport and emaSlope

//──────── VOLUME FILTER ────────
volFilter = volume > volMa * volMultiplier

//──────── RANGE / VOLATILITY FILTERS ────────
bodySize    = math.abs(close - open)
avgBody     = ta.sma(bodySize, 10)
strongCandle = bodySize > avgBody * 1.2

candleRange   = high - low
avgRange      = ta.sma(candleRange, 10)
rangeExpansion = candleRange > avgRange * 1.3

atr           = ta.atr(14)
atrExpansion  = atr > atr[1]

bbAvgWidth    = ta.sma(bbWidth, 10)
bbCompression = bbWidth < bbAvgWidth * 0.8
bbExpansion   = bbWidth > bbWidth[1] and bbWidth[1] >= bbWidth[2] and bbWidth[2] >= bbWidth[3]
bbFilter      = bbCompression or (bbExpansion and close > bbMiddle)

//──────── CANDLE QUALITY CONFIRMATION ────────
// Lightweight signal-specific candle checks. Purpose: confirm CE trend continues 5-8 candles.
// noUpperReject:    upper wick < body — sellers couldn't push back the reversal candle (DEEP)
// closeInUpperHalf: close > bar midpoint — buying pressure dominated entire candle (CONTINUATION)
// rangeExpansion:   already defined above — surge bar must be bigger than avg (ACCELERATION)
noUpperReject    = (high - close) < (close - open)
closeInUpperHalf = close > (high + low) / 2

//──────── RSI RECOVERY FILTER ────────
rsiRising   = ta.rising(rsi, 2)
// v8.0: removed overbought escape (rsi > 75). Always require rising RSI — overbought = fading.
rsiRecovery = rsi > rsiMin and rsiRising

//──────── MACD HISTOGRAM BURST SEQUENCE ────────
// shift candle: histogram flips negative→positive
// confirm candle: positive histogram >= histFloor (0.05 in v8.0 — any early positive candle)
// burst candle: positive histogram expands >= histBurstMultiplier× (1.5×)
histShiftPrevBar   = (macdHist[2] <= 0 and macdHist[1] > 0) or (macdHist[3] <= 0 and macdHist[2] > 0) or (macdHist[4] <= 0 and macdHist[3] > 0)
histConfirmCandle1 = macdHist[1] >= histFloor
histBurstCandle2   = macdHist > 0 and macdHist >= macdHist[1] * histBurstMultiplier and macdHist > macdHist[1]
// v8.0: replaced dead gate (open > close[1] — true 95% of bars) with real conviction check.
// bloomingCandle: bullish body with commitment (body ≥ avg), above EMA9, not at BB extreme.
bloomingCandle     = close > open and bodySize > avgBody * 1.0 and close > ema9
// Note: close < bbUpper removed — breakout candles legitimately pierce BB upper.
// stockNotOverextended (dayChange < 3%) already handles overbought fade risk.
priceBurstCandle2  = bloomingCandle
// Data-driven: vol CEILING prevents 9% WR disaster (MACD 0.3-0.5 + vol > 1.5x).
// Floor removed: early-session bars (09:15-09:30) are anchored to previous day's
// SMA(20), making any relative floor block structurally valid DEEP flips at open.
// deepContext + histBurstCandle2 + bloomingCandle provide quality without the floor.
volumeBurstCandle2 = volumeNotExcess
burstSequenceReady = histShiftPrevBar and histConfirmCandle1 and histBurstCandle2 and priceBurstCandle2 and volumeBurstCandle2

// continuationSequenceReady: fires when histogram already strong (> 0.60 floor, was 1.00 in v7.5).
// v8.0: 1.00 was too greedy — blocked chart-perfect DEEP setups where hist builds 0.2→0.4→0.65.
histContinuationCandle2   = macdHist > 0.60
// Volume in the sweet spot: above average but not in the panic-spike zone
continuationVolumeCandle2 = volume > volMa * 0.9 and volumeNotExcess
continuationSequenceReady = histContinuationCandle2 and priceBurstCandle2 and continuationVolumeCandle2

sequenceReady = burstSequenceReady or continuationSequenceReady

// sustainedHistRise: 3/4/5/6-bar rising alternatives — brief 1-bar MACD wobble
// in a genuine uptrend does not kill the signal. Requires histogram already positive.
histRise3      = ta.rising(macdHist, 3)
histRise4      = ta.rising(macdHist, 4)
histRise5      = ta.rising(macdHist, 5)
histRise6      = ta.rising(macdHist, 6)
sustainedHistRise = (histRise3 or histRise4 or histRise5 or histRise6) and macdHist > 0

// Preserve telemetry fields
histShiftCandle0       = histShiftPrevBar
macdLineConfirmCandle1 = macdLine[1] >= macdLine[2] and macdSignal[1] >= macdSignal[2]
rsiConfirmCandle1      = rsi > rsi[1]
volumeConfirmCandle1   = volumeBurstCandle2
emaConfirmCandle1      = priceBurstCandle2
vwapConfirmCandle1     = histConfirmCandle1
bbConfirmCandle1       = histConfirmCandle1
priceConfirmCandle1    = priceBurstCandle2
openStrengthCandle2    = priceBurstCandle2

deepContext            = macdLine[1] <= 0 and macdSignal[1] <= 0
accelerationContext    = macdLine[1] > 0 and macdSignal[1] > 0
neutralReversalContext = not deepContext and not accelerationContext

histVelocity  = histBurstCandle2

distanceFromEMA    = math.abs(close - ema9) / ema9 * 100
confirmDistanceFromEMA = math.abs(close[1] - ema9[1]) / ema9[1] * 100
notExtended        = distanceFromEMA < 1.5
confirmNotExtended = confirmDistanceFromEMA < 1.5
rsiDeepOversold    = rsi[2] < 45 or rsi[1] < 45
deepReversalSetup  = deepContext and sequenceReady

//──────── PRICE STRUCTURE & VWAP FILTER ────────
higherLow     = low > low[1] and low[1] >= low[2]
bullishClose  = close > open
vwapRising    = close > vwapVal and vwapVal > vwapVal[3]
// OR-based: accepts momentum on at least one dimension
priceStructure = (higherLow or bullishClose) and vwapRising

//──────── SESSION RISING FILTER ────────
// OR-based quality gate — accepts mid-session breakout stocks.
// Mirrors PUT v6 sessionBreakdownFilter which was the biggest PUT unlock.
intradayRisingStructure = macdHist > histFloor and emaTrendFlexible and vwapRising and close > ema20
sessionRisingFilter = priceStructure or (dayChange >= 0.20 and vwapRising and emaTrendFlexible and rsiRecovery) or (intradayRisingStructure and rsiRecovery)

//──────── TIME FILTER ────────
hourIST   = hour(time, "Asia/Kolkata")
minuteIST = minute(time, "Asia/Kolkata")
inTradeWindow = (hourIST == 9 and minuteIST >= 30) or (hourIST >= 10 and hourIST < 15) or (hourIST == 15 and minuteIST <= 0)

//──────── CONFIDENCE SCORING ────────
score = 0.0
score += neutralReversalContext ? 20 : 0
score += histShiftPrevBar       ? 20 : 0
score += histBurstCandle2       ? 25 : 0
score += macdHist > histFloor   ? 10 : 0
score += priceBurstCandle2      ? 15 : 0
score += volumeBurstCandle2     ? 10 : 0

deepScore = 0.0
deepScore += deepContext        ? 20 : 0
deepScore += histShiftPrevBar   ? 20 : 0
deepScore += histBurstCandle2   ? 25 : 0
deepScore += macdHist > histFloor ? 10 : 0
deepScore += priceBurstCandle2  ? 15 : 0
deepScore += volumeBurstCandle2 ? 10 : 0

//──────── MOMENTUM ACCELERATION ────────
momentumTrendStrict  = ema9[1] > ema20[1] and ema20[1] >= ema20[2] and close[1] > ema9[1]
momentumHistAccel    = histShiftCandle0 and histConfirmCandle1 and histVelocity
momentumRSI          = rsi[1] > 50 and rsi[1] > rsi[2]
momentumVolume       = volumeConfirmCandle1
momentumCandles      = close[1] > open[1] and close[1] >= close[2]
momentumVol          = atr[1] >= atr[2] or bbWidth[1] >= bbWidth[2]
momentumNotExtended  = confirmNotExtended and open < bbUpper
momentumAccelSetup   = accelerationContext and sequenceReady
// v9.2: sustained bypass — if hist already strong & rising (no flip needed for gap-up trending stocks)
accelHistValid       = momentumHistAccel or (continuationSequenceReady and sustainedHistRise and macdHistRising)

momScore = 0.0
momScore += accelerationContext ? 20 : 0
momScore += histShiftPrevBar    ? 20 : 0
momScore += histBurstCandle2    ? 25 : 0
momScore += macdHist > histFloor ? 10 : 0
momScore += priceBurstCandle2   ? 15 : 0
momScore += volumeBurstCandle2  ? 10 : 0

//──────── MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION SCORE ────────
// Fires on confirmed multi-bar uptrends — no MACD flip needed
contScore = 0.0
contScore += emaTrendStrict      ? 30 : (emaTrendFlexible ? 15 : 0)
contScore += sustainedHistRise   ? 20 : 0
contScore += vwapRising          ? 20 : 0
contScore += rsi > 60            ? 20 : (rsi > rsiMin ? 10 : 0)
// Data-driven: vol 1.2-1.5x sweet spot. Not using 1.5× floor — that's the danger zone.
contScore += (volume > volMa * 1.2 and volumeNotExcess) ? 10 : 0

//──────── ENTRY TRIGGERS ────────
priceAboveDayOpen = close > dayOpen

// v7.5: MACD_REVERSAL (neutral context) consistently loses at all hist levels (backtest: 9% WR).
// Replace with earlyPositiveContext — only the actual MACD zero-cross moment (bullish specific).
earlyPositiveContext = macdLine[1] > 0 and macdSignal[1] <= 0  // MACD line above 0, signal not yet
macdReversalSetup    = earlyPositiveContext and sequenceReady   // much stricter than neutralReversalContext

// v9.4: Simplified unified flip detection — same burst logic, context split by MACD territory.
// Replaces deepReversalTrigger complex gates + entire momentumAccelTrigger path.
// ═══ v9.13: UNIFIED EXPLOSIVE 2-TIER BURST — only 2 categories fire (DEEP + CONT) ═══
// candle-0 = macdHist[1] (first bloom, ≥ histFloor 0.05) ; candle-1 = macdHist (the fire bar).
//   Tier 1 STRONG  : candle-1 ≥ contStrongMult(2.0)× candle-0        → fire on candle-1 (immediate).
//   Tier 2 MARGINAL: candle-1 in [histBurstMultiplier(1.5)×, 2.0×)   → fire on candle-2 only if it holds.
// DEEP = shift from ≤0 (macdHist[2] <= 0). CONT (below) = same burst on the +ve side (macdHist[2] > 0).
// bloomingCandle (bullish body ≥ avg, close>ema9) is required inside each tier.
// v9.19: back to the flat histFloor (0.05) per literal spec — no price scaling. Simpler, and a low
// flat floor is trivially cleared right after a real flip, so it no longer delays the fire point.
deepBurstStrong   = macdHist[2] <= 0 and macdHist[1] >= histFloor and macdHist >= macdHist[1] * contStrongMult and macdHist > macdHist[1] and bloomingCandle
deepBurstDeferred = macdHist[3] <= 0 and macdHist[2] >= histFloor and macdHist[1] >= macdHist[2] * histBurstMultiplier and macdHist[1] < macdHist[2] * contStrongMult and macdHist >= macdHist[1] and bloomingCandle
deepBurstReady    = deepBurstStrong or deepBurstDeferred

// Shared ALL-RISING confluence (NO ceilings): RSI / Volume / EMA rising SHARPLY (2 bars) + VWAP rising.
// ADX = light flip-confirmation floor only (adxVal > 20). ADX is a smoothed lagging line; requiring it
// to RISE on candle-1/2 would veto the fresh burst we want (that was the v9.12 "ADX lags candle-2" note).
// Any one param flat/dipping ⇒ no trigger (kills the ULTRATECH-style "histogram peaked, params rolling over").
// v9.14: dropped volumeNotExcess (the 1.5-3.0× "chop band") from risingVol — per explicit spec this
// gate has NO ceiling; that band was blocking the exact 1.5-3x volume signature of a genuine ignition
// candle, which was measured as bad only on LATE (post-burst, chasing) entries, not fresh candle-1/2 ones.
// v9.19: confluence simplified to "building over the last 3 candles" (net change vs 3 bars ago),
// not a rigid bar-by-bar staircase. Tolerates normal 1-min noise while still confirming a real
// multi-candle build, per spec: "previous 3 candles RSI/VWAP/EMA/Volume building great".
// Volume kept OUT of the 3-bar "building" comparison: right at a MACD flip, volume is naturally choppy
// (sellers capitulating on one candle, buyers stepping in the next) — it spikes, it doesn't ramp
// smoothly like RSI/EMA/VWAP. What matters is the FIRE candle itself being genuinely elevated.
risingRSI  = rsi > rsi[3]
risingVol  = volume > volMa
risingEMA  = ema9 > ema9[3]
adxConfirm = adxVal > 20
risingAll  = risingRSI and risingVol and risingEMA and adxConfirm and vwapRising

deepReversalTrigger  = deepBurstReady and risingAll and priceAboveDayOpen and inTradeWindow and isExpectedTimeframe

// Legacy paths disabled (kept = false so the score/JSON blocks below still compile; only 2 categories fire).
earlyContFlipTrigger = false
momentumAccelTrigger = false

// MACD Reversal: disabled by default (enableMACDReversal=false).
// v7.5 backtest: consistently 5-9% WR at ALL hist levels, all context variations.
// earlyPositiveContext restricts to MACD zero-cross moment, but quality remains poor.
// Enable only for research/debugging.
macdReversalTrigger  = enableMACDReversal and macdReversalSetup and isExpectedTimeframe and not deepReversalTrigger and not momentumAccelTrigger and priceAboveDayOpen

// MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION: v8.0 redesign — mid-trend pullback resumption.
// Concept: stock already trending up (up on day), MACD briefly dips to zero/slightly negative,
// then resumes with the same 3-candle burst pattern as DEEP (but without deep context).
// This catches the "bloom" early — NOT late when histogram is already at 0.80+.
//
// v7.5 had macdHist >= 0.80 floor → fires late, enters fades.
// v8.0 uses burst detection → catches the re-acceleration at the earliest confirmation.
stockDayWinner    = not na(dayChange) and dayChange >= 0.25   // v8.0: was 0.50 — too strict on neutral days
// v9.7: STRICT consecutive 2-candle burst (was loose — histShiftPrevBar allowed the flip 1-3 bars
// back and the 0.05 floor sat on macdHist[1], so a weak 0.02 flip could drift up and fire late).
//   macdHist[2] <= 0      → flip happened EXACTLY 1 bar ago, so macdHist[1] IS the 1st bloom candle
//   macdHist[1] >= 0.05   → 1st-candle floor enforced on the real bloom candle
//   macdHist >= [1]*1.5 and > [1] → 2nd candle (current) is 1.5× and rising
// v9.10: TWO-TIER burst confirmation (replaces the single 1.5× candle-2 fire).
//   Notation: 1st bloom candle = macdHist[1] here (user's macdHist[0]); current bar = the fire bar.
//   Tier 1 (STRONG) — fire on the 2nd candle when it is >= contStrongMult (2×) the 1st bloom candle.
//     High-conviction burst → commit immediately.
//       macdHist[2]<=0 (flip 1 bar ago) · macdHist[1]>=0.05 (1st candle) · macdHist>=macdHist[1]*2 · rising
//   Tier 2 (MARGINAL) — the 2nd candle only "barely touched" 1.5×-2× the 1st → DON'T fire on candle 2;
//     wait one bar and fire on the 3rd candle only if it holds (macdHist >= the 2nd candle, no fizzle).
//       macdHist[3]<=0 (flip 2 bars ago) · macdHist[2]>=0.05 (1st candle) ·
//       macdHist[1] in [1.5×,2×) of macdHist[2] (the marginal 2nd candle) · macdHist>=macdHist[1] (3rd holds)
// v9.19: dropped the v9.16 dip-gate (macdHist[1] < macdHist[2]) — confirmed on SHREECEM it did NOT
// stop late/peak firing in practice, and it added complexity beyond spec. Back to the literal spec:
// CONT = the identical burst timing as DEEP, context split only by macdHist[2] > 0 (already an up-day),
// same flat histFloor.
contBurstStrong   = macdHist[2] > 0 and macdHist[1] >= histFloor and macdHist >= macdHist[1] * contStrongMult and macdHist > macdHist[1] and bloomingCandle
contBurstDeferred = macdHist[3] > 0 and macdHist[2] >= histFloor and macdHist[1] >= macdHist[2] * histBurstMultiplier and macdHist[1] < macdHist[2] * contStrongMult and macdHist >= macdHist[1] and bloomingCandle
contBurstReady    = contBurstStrong or contBurstDeferred
// stockDayWinner (up ≥0.25% on the day) kept — a continuation implies an existing up-day.
// DROPPED v9.13: contSustainedReady (the 3-bars-positive late path that fired ULTRATECH at the fade),
// stockNotOverextended, and all RSI/ADX ceilings. CONT now fires ONLY on the fresh candle-1/2 burst
// with every confluence param rising sharply — identical rules to DEEP, split only by macdHist[2] sign.
momentumContinuationTrigger = contBurstReady and risingAll and stockDayWinner and priceAboveDayOpen and inTradeWindow and isExpectedTimeframe and not deepReversalTrigger and not macdReversalTrigger

//──────── SIGNAL METRICS ────────
trend_strength  = ema9 - ema9[1]
rsi_expansion   = rsi - rsi[1]
momentum_score  = score
vol_expanding   = volFilter    ? 1 : 0
atr_expanding   = atrExpansion ? 1 : 0
hist_accelerating = histVelocity ? 1 : 0
range_expanding = rangeExpansion ? 1 : 0
price_extended  = notExtended  ? 0 : 1
volume_ratio    = volMa > 0   ? volume / volMa : 0.0
vwap_distance   = vwapVal > 0 ? (close - vwapVal) / vwapVal * 100 : 0.0
ema_spread      = ema20 > 0   ? (ema9 - ema20) / ema20 * 100 : 0.0
atr_pc          = close > 0   ? atr / close * 100 : 0.0

signal_confidence = macdReversalTrigger  ? math.max(75.0, math.min(90.0, score / 85.0 * 100.0)) : math.min(90.0, score / 85.0 * 100.0)
deep_confidence   = deepReversalTrigger  ? math.max(70.0, math.min(95.0,  deepScore / 75.0 * 100.0)) : math.min(95.0, deepScore / 75.0 * 100.0)
mom_confidence    = momentumAccelTrigger ? math.max(80.0, math.min(90.0,  momScore / 80.0 * 100.0)) : math.min(90.0, momScore / 80.0 * 100.0)
// v9.14 CRITICAL FIX: this floor was 75.0, but the bot's own OPTIONS_MIN_CONFIDENCE_MOMENTUM_CONTINUATION
// gate is 80 — EVERY genuine trigger was floored to exactly 75% and rejected at the door (confirmed live
// 2026-07-03: 320/320 rejections logged at precisely "75.0% < 80.0%", zero variance = the floor, not the
// score, was always the binding number). Raised to 88 (clears the 80 gate with headroom; a confirmed
// 1.5-2x+ burst with every param rising sharply is a high-conviction setup and should score as one).
cont_confidence   = momentumContinuationTrigger ? math.max(88.0, math.min(95.0, contScore)) : math.min(90.0, contScore)

market_trend_label = nifty50Change >= 0.5 ? "GOOD" : nifty50Change > -0.4 ? "NEUTRAL" : "BAD"
day_change         = prevDayClose > 0 ? (close - prevDayClose) / prevDayClose * 100 : na

//──────── ALERT JSON ────────
format_value(x) => str.tostring(x, format.mintick)

